## Content Insights

The main objective of this project was to create an informative website for **QuickBite Delivery**, an online food delivery platform that connects customers with local restaurants.

The website includes information about:

- Online food ordering.
- Fast and reliable delivery services.
- Multiple restaurant choices.
- Secure payment options.
- Restaurant categories available on the platform.
- The company's mission and goals.

During development, I learned the importance of organising website content into logical sections so visitors can quickly find the information they need. Using clear headings and concise descriptions also helped improve the overall readability of the website.

I also considered user experience by presenting the services and features in a simple and structured way rather than displaying large blocks of text.

---

## Career / Employability / Learning Insights

This activity improved my understanding of how websites should present information to users in a clear and organised manner. Although the website is relatively simple, it reinforced the importance of planning page structure before beginning development.

I also learned that good web design is not only about appearance but also about making information easy to understand and navigate. Organising content into meaningful sections helps improve the overall user experience and makes the website look more professional.

Through this project, I gained more confidence in designing websites that communicate a business idea effectively while applying good web design principles. These skills will be valuable when developing larger web applications and business websites in the future.
